WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:04.620
Prime Day has come and gone, and there's more
of July behind us than in front of us.

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:08.820
It's time to take a look at the new offerings
you should keep your eyes open for on Amazon

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:10.840
Prime Video in August 2019.

00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:16.270
Amazon Prime's new original series Carnival
Row mixes fantasy, mystery, and a politically

00:00:16.270 --> 00:00:20.780
tense environment that, for some people at
least, feels all too familiar at this point.

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:25.860
Starring Orlando Bloom as human Rycroft Philostrate
and Cara Delevingne as as the winged faerie

00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:31.070
Vignette Stonemoss, Carnival Row is set in
a Victorian-era city where the kinds of fantasy

00:00:31.070 --> 00:00:35.070
creatures we're not used to seeing outside
of The Lord of the Rings or a Dungeons &amp; Dragons

00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:37.460
campaign are an everyday fact of life.

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:40.620
Kind of like that Bright movie, but maybe…
y'know.

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:41.180
Better.

00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:43.480
"Fairy lives don't matter today."

00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:48.360
But while these creatures' existences are
accepted, that doesn't mean the humans of

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:50.460
this fictional world like them very much.

00:00:50.790 --> 00:00:55.440
The fantasy creatures of Carnival Row - like
Vignette - are refugees from a war-torn land,

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:58.660
and are subjected to inhumane laws while living
in the city.

00:00:59.210 --> 00:01:03.340
One freedom denied them is romance with humans,
making the affair between Rycroft and Vignette

00:01:03.340 --> 00:01:04.260
a risky one.

00:01:04.740 --> 00:01:09.040
While the pair wrestle with that looming danger,
they must also investigate a string of unsolved

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:09.540
murders.

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:14.340
All eight hourlong episodes of Carnival Row
will be released on Amazon Prime on August

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:14.880
30.

00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:19.060
With a premise so unique and promising, it
definitely looks to be worth checking out.

00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:23.340
If the trailer for next year's Top Gun: Maverick
got your blood pumping, but you don't want

00:01:23.350 --> 00:01:28.310
to wait until 2020 to see Tom Cruise in action,
Amazon Prime might have a partial solution

00:01:28.310 --> 00:01:28.800
for you.

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:34.860
On August 23, 2018's critically-lauded Mission:
Impossible - Fallout lands on the service,

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:38.520
featuring starring turns from Cruise, Henry
Cavill, and Ving Rhames.

00:01:38.990 --> 00:01:43.300
Cavill's career owes a lot to Zack Snyder,
who directed the actor as comic book icon

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:48.040
Superman in Man of Steel, Batman v. Superman:
Dawn of Justice, and Justice League.

00:01:48.280 --> 00:01:52.260
And Amazon Prime might be a favorite place
for Zack Snyder fans in August.

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:57.940
Snyder's Persian War epic 300 will be Prime's
very first new August arrival, with his original

00:01:57.940 --> 00:02:00.060
story Sucker Punch arriving later in the month.

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:04.600
While none of Snyder's superhero flicks will
arrive on Prime in August, Guillermo del Toro's

00:02:04.610 --> 00:02:08.649
Hellboy II: The Golden Army will be there,
and it will be joined by other monster-filled

00:02:08.649 --> 00:02:13.909
action flicks like 2014's Godzilla and the
Aaron Eckhart-led graphic novel adaptation

00:02:13.909 --> 00:02:15.120
I, Frankenstein.

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:19.319
The process of buying a home isn't known for
its lack of stress.

00:02:19.319 --> 00:02:22.319
But if you find yourself looking for a new
place to hang your hat and find the whole

00:02:22.319 --> 00:02:27.879
thing impossibly frustrating, maybe drop by
Amazon Prime at the end of August for 1986's

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:30.720
horror sequel Poltergeist II: The Other Side.

00:02:30.980 --> 00:02:35.580
Starring Craig T. Nelson, JoBeth Williams,
and Heather O'Rourke, Poltergeist II is the

00:02:35.590 --> 00:02:40.160
second entry in the saga of the Freeling family
- people who just can't get a break when it

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:42.020
comes to where they plant their stakes.

00:02:42.349 --> 00:02:47.099
Though they've moved from the home where vengeful
spirits plagued them in 1982's Poltergeist,

00:02:47.099 --> 00:02:50.790
the family soon learns the truth of the old
adage, "No matter where you go… there the

00:02:50.790 --> 00:02:52.500
creepy ghosts from the first movie are."

00:02:56.820 --> 00:02:57.780
"They're back…"

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:03.349
But if supernatural fears aren't your cup
of tea, Amazon is also offering some scares

00:03:03.349 --> 00:03:07.940
based more firmly in the real world with 2013's
Manuscripts Don't Burn.

00:03:08.390 --> 00:03:13.200
Made by Iranian filmmaker Mohammad Rasoulof,
the thriller follows a writer named Kasra

00:03:13.209 --> 00:03:18.590
as he attempts to escape Iran with his politically-charged
writing after the country's authorities learn

00:03:18.590 --> 00:03:19.080
of his plans.

00:03:22.040 --> 00:03:27.839
In 1996, former US Director of Central Intelligence
William Colby disappeared under mysterious

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:28.680
circumstances.

00:03:29.020 --> 00:03:33.820
Fifteen years later, a documentary was released
called The Man Nobody Knew: In Search of My

00:03:33.820 --> 00:03:39.100
Father, CIA Spymaster William Colby, directed
and narrated by the late Colby's son Carl.

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:43.951
Driven by a son's need to know the truth about
his father and inevitably tied to some of

00:03:43.951 --> 00:03:48.569
the most important historical events of the
20th century, The Man Nobody Knew succeeds

00:03:48.569 --> 00:03:53.340
as what Philadelphia Inquirer's Steven Rea
calls, quote, "a deeply personal film and

00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:55.100
an important historical document."

00:03:55.540 --> 00:03:58.740
The documentary arrives on Amazon Prime on
August 31.

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:03.760
If you'd prefer something with a bit more
distance from the present day, 1983's western

00:04:03.760 --> 00:04:06.120
drama Sacred Ground premieres the same day.

00:04:06.460 --> 00:04:11.499
The film is noteworthy both a rare western
produced in the 1980s, well after the popularity

00:04:11.500 --> 00:04:12.760
of the genre had faded.

00:04:13.160 --> 00:04:17.599
It's also the final film of character actor
Tim McIntire, a recognizable "oh, it's that

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:19.520
guy" of the 60s and 70s.

00:04:19.989 --> 00:04:24.580
Set the same year the American Civil War began,
Sacred Ground revolves around the ostracism

00:04:24.580 --> 00:04:29.080
that a white man and Native American woman
face when they choose to live as man and wife.

00:04:29.720 --> 00:04:33.780
If you need some more laughter in your life,
Amazon Prime is serving up some uniquely humorous

00:04:33.780 --> 00:04:34.920
offerings in August.

00:04:35.300 --> 00:04:39.120
The indy comedy Computer Chess shows up on
Prime at the end of the month, and if you

00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:43.500
haven't seen it, it's well worth a look - 2013's
critics couldn't get enough of it.

00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:49.100
Filmed completely on analog video and, as
The AV Club's Mike D'Angelo put it, having

00:04:49.110 --> 00:04:53.560
the look of an industrial training film from
the '80s, Computer Chess unfolds over a weekend

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:57.710
summit of computer chess programmers - the
kind of smart tech people who helped create

00:04:57.710 --> 00:04:59.080
the world we live in now.

00:04:59.300 --> 00:05:03.340
If you find yourself enjoying that style of
quirky, nerdy humor, keep things going by

00:05:03.340 --> 00:05:08.930
following an atomic scientist to a town full
of people-eating salesmen in 1999's comedy-horror

00:05:08.930 --> 00:05:09.860
Top of the Food Chain.

00:05:11.140 --> 00:05:12.260
"Some kind of monster."

00:05:12.940 --> 00:05:14.220
"What the heck are you guys shooting at?"

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:18.280
But if you don't want to spend a weekend simply
nerding out, you can instead spend some time

00:05:18.289 --> 00:05:22.729
with Anna Kendrick and Blake Lively in the
twisted black comedy mystery movie A Simple

00:05:22.729 --> 00:05:23.220
Favor.

00:05:23.320 --> 00:05:24.360
"What were you saying about me being a f---ing
psycho?"

00:05:24.560 --> 00:05:29.080
Or, for something a little sweeter and more
family-friendly, watch as Michael Keaton dies

00:05:29.100 --> 00:05:32.560
and comes back to life as a snowman in 1998's
Jack Frost.

00:05:33.980 --> 00:05:34.600
"Hey Charlie.

00:05:34.940 --> 00:05:36.680
Thanks for giving me a second chance to be
your dad."

00:05:37.060 --> 00:05:41.200
Staying in with that high-concept movie won't
just give you a weird blast of nostalgia;

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:44.820
it can also help take your mind off just how
hot it is outside.

00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:47.320
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:05:47.400 --> 00:05:50.880
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
movies are coming soon.

00:05:51.080 --> 00:05:54.360
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

